            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a trick, then the Hindi for an effort, an endeavour (formal)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: रुकावट",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुकावट — rukāvaṭ — \"an obstacle, a hold-up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सड़क पर एक पेड़ गिरा था, इसलिए रास्ते में रुकावट थी। Saṛak par ek peṛ girā thā, isliye rāste meṁ rukāvaṭ thī. A tree had fallen on the road, so the way was blocked."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रुकावट (rukāvaṭ) is the noun of ruknā, \"to stop\", which CDIAL lists beside roknā under a reconstructed rokk (CDIAL 10827), with the ending -āvaṭ that makes nouns of verbs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
